[{:db/id 17592186157249 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-b9cdc646-22ad-53d7-894a-78ecf8a59507"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-b9cdc646-22ad-53d7-894a-78ecf8a59507" :question/id #uuid "b9cdc646-22ad-53d7-894a-78ecf8a59507" :question/math-academy-id "q-160633" :question/problem "![](images/5f/5f91cc8b30f9b764021cd84c374a328c7ffb1287a9f0dc6a211a3fadfac2fdbd.png)\n\nConsider the square region $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane, given by\n\n$$\nΔ={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le 1}\n$$\n\nand the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (x(u,v),y(u,v)),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\nx={u}^{2},\\,y=uv.\n$$\n\nFind the image of $Δ$ under the action of $T.$ \n\n*Hint: You may assume that $T$ has no critical points in the interior of $Δ.$*" :question/worked-solution "We're told that $T$ has no critical points in the interior of $Δ.$ So, to map the entire region $Δ$ onto the $xy$-plane, we transform each side of $Δ$ separately:\n\n- Consider the image of the side ${S}_{1},$ where we have $v=0$ and $0\\le u\\le 1.$ Substituting $v=0$ into our transformation equations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x,y) & =T(u,v) &  \\\\  & =({u}^{2},\\,uv) &  \\\\  & =({u}^{2},\\,u(0)) &  \\\\  & =({u}^{2},\\,0), & 0\\le u\\le 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is a horizontal line segment traversed from the point $(0,0)$ to the point $(1,0)$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\n- Consider the image of the side ${S}_{2}.$ Here, we have $u=1$ and $0\\le v\\le 1.$ Substituting $u=1$ into our transformation equations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x,y) & =T(u,v) &  \\\\  & =({u}^{2},\\,uv) &  \\\\  & =({1}^{2},\\,1v) &  \\\\  & =(1,\\,v), & 0\\le v\\le 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is a vertical line segment traversed from the point $(1,0)$ to the point $(1,1)$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\n- Consider the image of the side ${S}_{3}.$ Here, we have $v=1$ and $1\\ge u\\ge 0.$ Substituting $v=1$ into our transformation equations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x,y) & =T(u,v) &  \\\\  & =({u}^{2},\\,uv) &  \\\\  & =({u}^{2},\\,u(1)) &  \\\\  & =({u}^{2},\\,u), & 1\\ge u\\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is a right-opening parabola traversed from the point $(1,1)$ to the point $(0,0)$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\n- Consider the image of the side ${S}_{4}.$ Here, we have $u=0$ and $1\\ge v\\ge 0.$ Substituting $u=0$ into our transformation equations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x,y) & =T(u,v) &  \\\\  & =({u}^{2},\\,uv) &  \\\\  & =({0}^{2},\\,0v) &  \\\\  & =(0,\\,0), & 1\\ge v\\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nThis is the point $(0,0)$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\nDrawing the images of the sides of our square, we obtain the following image of $Δ:$\n\n![](images/cf/cfcee7d6c19b748385a35291ab582e7ce0dace9a1207d014b64165caa6d3bc2a.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1b03f791-a25e-5d56-8bc4-3d32145b2ec9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1b03f791-a25e-5d56-8bc4-3d32145b2ec9" :answer-field/id #uuid "1b03f791-a25e-5d56-8bc4-3d32145b2ec9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-59020315-291c-59c3-9224-961256ce3b94" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ac5779ec-3893-54d8-8fd5-cb71c18cf754" "answer-5cdefaa7-89d2-5114-a2e1-0fce719d5db3" "answer-9dcdde3a-a348-5fc5-968e-c1ee5b390866" "answer-5d5ebdc7-9d12-52cf-8d15-a55e4c96ac2b" "answer-59020315-291c-59c3-9224-961256ce3b94"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ac5779ec-3893-54d8-8fd5-cb71c18cf754" :answer/id #uuid "ac5779ec-3893-54d8-8fd5-cb71c18cf754" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/16/166fff724178c7285d6256c5b6f68c4181b66c246426e75759e196b2f2b3c0a9.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5cdefaa7-89d2-5114-a2e1-0fce719d5db3" :answer/id #uuid "5cdefaa7-89d2-5114-a2e1-0fce719d5db3" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/21/217244e03a7f3eb3d47d936a337de962d680d477ed944a75f7e74d426b53ff8a.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9dcdde3a-a348-5fc5-968e-c1ee5b390866" :answer/id #uuid "9dcdde3a-a348-5fc5-968e-c1ee5b390866" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/2c/2c1d6e726da49ac8c398357ee00cbb53706a13a6baec25d35a3c594192d804eb.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5d5ebdc7-9d12-52cf-8d15-a55e4c96ac2b" :answer/id #uuid "5d5ebdc7-9d12-52cf-8d15-a55e4c96ac2b" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/a6/a60a2532e8cfea8044ddc5e52ef65a8fc83808fc8d35217130d243fe77e8c350.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-59020315-291c-59c3-9224-961256ce3b94" :answer/id #uuid "59020315-291c-59c3-9224-961256ce3b94" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/cf/cfcee7d6c19b748385a35291ab582e7ce0dace9a1207d014b64165caa6d3bc2a.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186157247 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-aedbf0c6-276b-509d-933d-5c28129e8de2"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-aedbf0c6-276b-509d-933d-5c28129e8de2" :question/id #uuid "aedbf0c6-276b-509d-933d-5c28129e8de2" :question/math-academy-id "q-225139" :question/problem "![](images/33/33e48fa5bdbb034bcf489e038ccf80fc5f67baabeccacc1b7abd741183ebf05d.png)\n\nConsider the square region $Δ$ and its **directed** boundary $∂Δ$ in the $uv$-plane, where $Δ$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔ={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le 1},\n$$\n\nand the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (x(u,v),y(u,v)),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\nx=2{v}^{2}+u,\\,y=u-{v}^{4}.\n$$\n\nThe image of the side ${S}_{3}$ under the action of $T$ is a **directed** line segment. Find the endpoints of this segment, stated in the order that they are traversed." :question/worked-solution "To map the entire region $Δ$ onto the $xy$-plane, we consider the transformation of each side. However, in this case, we consider only the side ${S}_{3}.$\n\nFor the side ${S}_{3},$ we have $v=1$ and $1\\ge u\\ge 0.$ Substituting $v=1$ into our transformation equations, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x,y) & =T(u,v) \\\\  & =(2{v}^{2}+u,\\,u-{v}^{4}) \\\\  & =(2(1)^{2}+u,\\,u-{1}^{4}) \\\\  & =(2+u,\\,u-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the image of ${S}_{3}$ can be parametrized by\n\n$$\nx=2+u,\\,y=u-1,\\,1\\ge u\\ge 0.\n$$\n\n \n\nWriting this in the usual notation, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)=2+t,\\,y(t)=t-1,\\,1\\ge t\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nThis is a line segment with endpoints $(3,0)$ and $(2,-1)$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\n![](images/2a/2ac0e0eac9e4633a8d29881782d8dfe93c4c594ca0f99912a98507822c97c4b4.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d47620cc-ff04-5478-975c-18645160652a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d47620cc-ff04-5478-975c-18645160652a" :answer-field/id #uuid "d47620cc-ff04-5478-975c-18645160652a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e6c04fe0-8935-5aff-a0db-580177fae6a8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-31e82cf1-a965-5d27-8faf-45515b67a2ed" "answer-3d9762f5-d942-5b02-90e1-433937835992" "answer-8f7d123e-9efa-5d77-821b-8c45d6d2e441" "answer-758ca0b2-013b-5d8c-a6a5-3ac1ce65e6a2" "answer-e6c04fe0-8935-5aff-a0db-580177fae6a8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-31e82cf1-a965-5d27-8faf-45515b67a2ed" :answer/id #uuid "31e82cf1-a965-5d27-8faf-45515b67a2ed" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(-1,2)$ and $(0,3)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3d9762f5-d942-5b02-90e1-433937835992" :answer/id #uuid "3d9762f5-d942-5b02-90e1-433937835992" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(0,3)$ and $(-1,2)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8f7d123e-9efa-5d77-821b-8c45d6d2e441" :answer/id #uuid "8f7d123e-9efa-5d77-821b-8c45d6d2e441" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(2,-1)$ and $(3,0)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-758ca0b2-013b-5d8c-a6a5-3ac1ce65e6a2" :answer/id #uuid "758ca0b2-013b-5d8c-a6a5-3ac1ce65e6a2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(3,-1)$ and $(0,2)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e6c04fe0-8935-5aff-a0db-580177fae6a8" :answer/id #uuid "e6c04fe0-8935-5aff-a0db-580177fae6a8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(3,0)$ and $(2,-1)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-23a36746-618b-5408-8fcd-c638b93c9f28" :activity/id #uuid "23a36746-618b-5408-8fcd-c638b93c9f28" :activity/title "Nonlinear Transformations of Plane Regions" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186049373 :activity/course 17592186046659 :activity/steps ["step-c4aa2659-822f-5c81-9961-6d81d19483c6" "step-283e81ba-165c-5712-b058-a61afb12269f" "step-526a1df8-1606-5e36-8deb-549a340f512b" "step-bc6691b7-166a-5089-867e-8ee8a5dc5783" "step-ba6262b9-b0fe-5e23-a4c4-b3dd83e994ec"] :activity/first-step "step-c4aa2659-822f-5c81-9961-6d81d19483c6" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-c4aa2659-822f-5c81-9961-6d81d19483c6" :step/id #uuid "c4aa2659-822f-5c81-9961-6d81d19483c6" :step/content 17592186389063 :step/next "step-283e81ba-165c-5712-b058-a61afb12269f" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-283e81ba-165c-5712-b058-a61afb12269f" :step/id #uuid "283e81ba-165c-5712-b058-a61afb12269f" :step/content "question-b9cdc646-22ad-53d7-894a-78ecf8a59507" :step/next "step-526a1df8-1606-5e36-8deb-549a340f512b" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-526a1df8-1606-5e36-8deb-549a340f512b" :step/id #uuid "526a1df8-1606-5e36-8deb-549a340f512b" :step/content "question-aedbf0c6-276b-509d-933d-5c28129e8de2" :step/next "step-bc6691b7-166a-5089-867e-8ee8a5dc5783" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-bc6691b7-166a-5089-867e-8ee8a5dc5783" :step/id #uuid "bc6691b7-166a-5089-867e-8ee8a5dc5783" :step/content 17592186290422 :step/next "step-ba6262b9-b0fe-5e23-a4c4-b3dd83e994ec" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-ba6262b9-b0fe-5e23-a4c4-b3dd83e994ec" :step/id #uuid "ba6262b9-b0fe-5e23-a4c4-b3dd83e994ec" :step/content 17592186290425 :db/ensure [:step/validate]}]
